-- drop: drop the first n elements from a list.
-- Written as an arrow graph over list primitives.
-- Contract: inferred from the loop body.
--
-- Graph structure:
--   drop = loop(arr("list.tail") >>> first(id))
--
-- The loop processes elements one at a time:
--   - take the tail of the remaining input (drop one element)
--   - the counter (side channel) passes through unchanged via first(id)
--   - repeat until n elements are dropped

drop = loop(arr("list.tail") >>> first(id))
